Example: alpha-Al2O3 (corundum), space group R-3c (167), point group -3m (trigonal I).
The POSCAR is the 10-atom primitive rhombohedral cell with c (3-fold axis) along z and
a along x; for R-3c that puts x on a 2-fold axis, so trigonal_1 is valid here.
trigonal_2 works too (one extra deformation set) and is the safe choice in general.

copy POTCAR (Al, O, in that order) from your vasp-package to start this example (example doesnot contain POTCAR)
make sure INCAR POTCAR POSCAR KPOINTS exist
Edit your test.py and strain.dat if require
uncomment eg.trigonal_2_pre() (or eg.trigonal_1_pre())
run python3 test.py
This will generate the folders C11_C12_I C11_C12_II C11_C33_C13_I C11_C33_C13_II
C11_C44_C14_I C11_C44_C14_II (and C11_C44_C15 for trigonal_2)
Each folder contain different strain folder
copy INCAR KPOINTS POTCAR and run.pbs into each strain folder inside each folder
you can use copy.sh for copying and running vasp also
Once each folder calculation complete
edit test.py and uncomment post-processing constants.trigonal_2_post() (or trigonal_1_post();
don't forget to comment pre-processing one)
you are done
